 { White is a pawn up, but with such a passive king it is difficult for him to aspire at anything. With his next move Granda addresses this issue. } 1. { -KEY- } g5 $1 { This advance doesn't just creates a passed pawn on the h-file, it also clears a path for the king towards the shelter on e6. } Rh1+ ( { After } 1... hxg5 2. Kxg5 Rg1 ( { or } 2... e4 3. h6 { and the h-pawn costs Black a rook } ) 
3. Kf6 { followed by 4 Ke6, White wins at once. } ) 
 ( { Neither does } 1... Rf4 { make sense, in view of } 2. Kg3 hxg5 3. h6 Rh4 4. h7 { and the threat of } -- 5. h8=Q Rxh8 6. Ra8 { again decides. } ) 
2. Kg4 hxg5 ( { Or } 2... Rg1 3. Kf5 Rxg5 4. Ke6 { winning - Granda. } ) 
3. Rh7 $1 { A key move to liberate the king from the defence of the h-pawn. } ( { The immediate } 3. Kf5 $2 { permits } Rxh5 4. Ke6 Rh6 5. Kd5 Rh1 $1 6. Kc6 ( 6. Rg7 { preparing 7 Rg6, is useless as Black can play the move ...Kd7 once the white rook leaves the seventh rank } ) 
Rc1 7. Kd5 Rh1 $1 { neutralizing the shelter idea. } ) 
 ( { Probably } 3. Kxg5 { works too: } e4 4. Re7 $1 ( { but not } 4. h6 $2 e3 5. Re7 Rg1 6. Kf6 Rf1 7. Kg7 Rg1 8. Kh8 Rg3 9. h7 Kc8 { and White seems unable to progress; e.g. } 10. Rg7 e2 $1 11. Re7 Rg2 { etc } ) 
Rg1 5. Kf5 e3 ( { or } 5. Rh7 Rh1 6. Rh7 e3 7. Ke6 ) 
6. Rxe3 Rh1 7. Kg6 Rg1 8. Kh7 Kd7 9. Rd3 Rg2 10. h6 Rg1 11. Kh8 Rg2 12. h7 Rg1 13. Ra3 { and White wins by Ra8-g8 followed by the king's withdrawal. Anyway, Granda's solution is much more clear-cut. } ) 
e4 ( { After } 3... Rd1 4. h6 Rxd6 5. Rh8 { followed by 6 h7, White wins by one tempo. } ) 
4. Kf5 $1 e3 5. Ke6 { The shelter is ready, and Black can only rely on desperate moves. } Kc8 6. d7+ Kc7 7. Ke7 $1 ( { Avoiding the trap } 7. Rh8 Rd1 8. Rc8 Kb7 9. d8=Q $4 ( { although } 9. Rc2 { wins as well } ) 
Rxd8 10. Rxd8 e2 ) 
Rd1 8. Ke8 ( { In view of the inevitable } 9. d8Q { , Black resigned. } ) 

