 { Usually the shelter works in combination with a passed pawn, but it can also have other functions, as in the following, thrilling example. Black is a pawn down but his pieces are very active. Kasparov finds a brilliant idea. } 1... { -KEY- } Kc3 $1 { Instead of capturing any of the enemy pawns, Black approaches his king in order to create a mating net. For this idea to work, the d4-pawn must evidently remain on the board. } 2. Qd8 $2 ( { Defending the d4-pawn is not the highest priority in this sharp position. } 2. b5 $1 { was a more active try, in order to create a passed pawn on the a-file or in the center. Stohl gives the sample variation } Qxd4 3. Kf3 Qd5 4. Kf2 axb5 5. Qc8 { preparing a5-a6. } ) 
 ( 2. Qg5 $5 { attacking the h5-pawn was another good choice, for example, } Qxd4 3. Kf3 Kxb4 { ( } f4 4. Qxf4 { makes no sense for Black, while if } Qg4 { White simply moves their king, finally } Qxe5 { allows } 4. Qxh5 { ) } 4. Qe7 { (of course not } 4. Qxh5 $4 Qd1 { ) } Kc3 5. Qxe6 { and the e-pawn is strong enough to secure a draw, as observed by Farciarz. } ) 
Qd3+ 3. Kf4 ( { Probably } 3. Kf2 { was better, although after } f4 $1 4. Qg5 Qxd4 5. Ke2 Qd2 6. Kf1 Qe3 { Black should win' - Stohl. } ) 
Qd2+ ( { Kasparov also suggests } 3... Kd2 $5 4. Kg5 f4 $1 { when the pawn is immune due to mate and its further advance can't be easily parried. } ) 
 ( { Of course } 3... Qxd4 $4 4. Qxd4 Kxd4 5. b5 { wasn't Black's idea. } ) 
4. Kf3 Qd1+ 5. Ke3 ( { Or } 5. Kf2 f4 $1 6. Qc8 Kd2 { followed by a check on either e2 or g3-h4, after which the ...f5-f4-f3 advance decides. } ) 
Qg1+ $1 { The mating net is taking shape. } 6. Ke2 ( { Obviously, } 6. Kf4 { fails to } Kd3 { e.g. } 7. Kf3 f4 $1 8. Qg5 Qf1 ) 
 ( { while after } 6. Kf3 Qf1 7. Ke3 ( { or } 7. Kg3 f4 8. Kh2 Qe2 9. Kh1 f3 10. Qg5 f2 { and the passed pawn takes its toll; } ) 
f4 8. Ke4 Kd2 $1 { Black gives mate on d3-e3 - Stohl. } ) 
Qg2+ 7. Ke3 ( { White is also mated after } 7. Ke1 Kd3 ) 
f4+ $1 ( { In view of } 7... f4 8. Kxf4 Kd3 $1 9. Qg5 Qf2 { White resigned. } ) 

 0-1
